 role wasn't finished just yet and  he still holds some important  information that is yet to be revealed  but I believe he will find it in some of  those books or documents he took from  the Citadel with Sam's help they will  find a way to survive the greatest  threat the realm has ever known Arya  Stark was just as little girl who wanted  to learn how to water dance and protect  herself but now she has become this  badass ninja assassin who holds one of  the few Valyrian steel weapons that will  be used to take down some of the White  Walkers her skill set should be very  useful in the war to come and I can't  forget about Tyrion the IMP Lannister it  seemed like this man was destined to end  up like Robert Baratheon just drinking  and whoring his way through life but  look at him now he ran into some bumps  along the road during season 7 but he  did earn his hand to the Queen title  unlike when he was hand to the king  during his father's absence although he  did prove he could handle the job when  need be he also earned his stripes  during the Battle of Blackwater Bay  and I think Tyrians advising and war  tactics should be vital during the war  against the night king ginjury was also  just another bass  that seemed like he would be a  dime-a-dozen blacksmith for the rest of  his life or roaming the woods with the  Brotherhood without banners but after he  disappeared for multiple seasons he  found his way back into the main plot  ginjury was brought back for a reason  and it must have something to do with  his skills as a blacksmith or bringing  together houses Stark and Baratheon  after the war is over  Gendry will be needed to ensure that  house Baratheon does not go extinct and  before it's all said and done he could  end up in a very powerful position now  that the Hound is back he has seen the  light and his services are gonna be used  for something good the Hound is gonna be  a strong soldier for this war and I  can't wait to see him kick some white  Walker ass hopefully he does get his  hands on some Valyrian steel something  he said he has always wanted but  regardless if he does or not the  Brotherhood without banners were right  the Lord of Light isn't done with the  hounds just yet and his role is just  getting started  I loved watching this episode again now  knowing with hindsight just how  important these cripples bastards and  broken things really are at first glance  most of these characters were being  overlooked and I love underdog stories I  love seeing characters rise to greatness  that once had no business of being in  any position to do so but I am going to  assume Dan and Dave will keep the  essence of George RR Martin's story and  give this a bittersweet ending so we  could see some significant losses before  it's all said and done one of the most  popular phrases in this story as all men  must die so even though these characters  will play their important roles it  doesn't necessarily mean they will  survive the winter  but these cripples bastards and broken  things will all leave their marks on  this world they will end up being more  important to the survival of the realm  than all of the other kings queens lords  and ladies who look down on them for  most of their lives and who knows maybe  the theory about Sam being the narrator  of this story is true and if it is true  and we do see Sam as an old man reading  or writing down the final pages of this  moment in time then I am confident he  will give these characters their proper  time to shine on the pages knowing they  stepped up in the most dire of  situations to do what they could to save  the realm in possibly even sacrificing  themselves to ensure that others would  survive  that could be a better sweet ending in  itself or at least it would be for me  but of course we are going to need  several armies in several large dragons  to fight the night king but without the  prep work done by characters like John  bran Sam and even Tyrion none of